\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Bank of Israel buys over $600 mln of  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2009\par 14:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Bank of Israel buys over $600 mln in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Shekel weakens 0.6 percent against dollar\par \par \uc2 * Euro gains 1.6 percent against shekel\par \par \uc2 (Releads with new figure, adds quotes, official rate)\par \par \uc2 By Tova Cohen\par \par \uc2 TEL AVIV, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The shekel weakened around 0.6 percent against the dollar on Tuesday as the Bank of Israel bought over $600 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a dealer at an Israeli bank said.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Israel bought a lot today, over $600 million," the dealer told Reuters, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 In the morning a dealer at \uc2 Israel Discount Bank\uc2  estimated the Bank of Israel had bought $100 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved the dollar up to 3.77 shekels from 3.74," the Discount dealer told Reuters right after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yet despite the very heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in the day, the shekel only depreciated a little bit more as the dollar weakened globally, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The shekel's official rate was set at 3.780 per dollar, compared with a rate of 3.7570 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The euro gained 1.6 percent to 5.4784 shekels per euro.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from time to time to prevent a further appreciation of the shekel, which would hurt exporters.\par \par \uc2 In August the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $4.073 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market.\par \par \uc2 "It appears that massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $4 billion a month cannot continue over time," Michael Sarel, head of economic research at Harel Finance, wrote in a report on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Harel forecast the exchange rate against the dollar will be basically unchanged in six months at 3.76.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel last month halted a more than one-year programme of buying $100 million a day in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on days of "unusual movements" in the market.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in August after it raised its key short-term borrowing rate by a quarter point to 0.75 percent. [ID:nLO650919]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  right before and after the surprising rate hike.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tova Cohen; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-SHEKEL/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090908e598000yt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
