\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Shekel up on rate hike; emerging shares down\b0\par\par\uc2 726 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2009\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * MSCI emerging market stocks down 0.5 pct\par \par \uc2 * Israeli shekel higher after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate hike\par \par \uc2 * Hungary's forint lower after rate cuts\par \par \uc2 * Weaker commodities weigh on rand, rouble\par \par \uc2 By Natsuko Waki\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Aug 25 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Tuesday, a day after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised markets by raising interest rates, defying a broader decline in emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's forint inched lower after its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  delivered a second cut in key interest rates in two months and said more cuts could come to ease a deep recession. Israel's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised short-term borrowing costs by a quarter point on Monday to 0.75 percent to rein in inflation, making it the first among developed and key emerging-economy central banks to tighten monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The shekel's rise comes despite a recent spate of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in again on Monday, with one saying that the bank bought $130-140 million worth of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The hike in Israeli interest rates has raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk in the shekel in the near term," said Benoit Anne, EMEA \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt strategist at Bank of America Securities-Merrill Lynch.\par \par \uc2 "The underlying fundamentals of the shekel are much stronger and, to compensate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be more active in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but the shekel should continue to appreciate despite some volatility."\par \par \uc2 The shekel rose 0.3 percent to 3.7880 per dollar <ILS=>.\par \par \uc2 The forint fell 0.1 percent to 268.10 per euro <EURHUF=>. Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the cost of borrowing down by half a point to 8 percent. Tuesday's data showed the country's retail sales fell 2.2 percent in June, underscoring weak personal spending.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's benchmark emerging market stocks <.MSCIEF> fell 0.5 percent, following the world index <.MIWD00000PUS> which lost 0.4 percent from Monday's 10-month high.\par \par \uc2 Chinese stocks <.SSEC> fell 2.6 percent after cautious remarks from Premier Wen Jiabao late on Monday prompted concerns about possible slowing in the country's economic recovery. Emerging Asian stocks <.MIAPJ0000PUS> fell 0.7 percent.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices <CLc1> fell 0.7 percent to $73.87 a barrel, weighing on resource \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the South African rand <ZAR=> which fell one-third of a percent to 7.80 per dollar and the Russian rouble <RUS=MCX>, which fell a quarter percent against its euro-dollar basket.\par \par \uc2 CORPORATE BOND ISSUANCE UP\par \par \uc2 Emerging market bond spreads widened 1 basis point to trade 367 bps over U.S. Treasuries <11EMJ>.\par \par \uc2 Royal Bank of Canada Capital Markets said a resurgence of corporate bond issuance from emerging markets pushed the year-to-date total amount to $104 billion, exceeding the total for the whole of 2008 and approaching the historical peak of $197 billion reached in 2007 on an annualised basis.\par \par \uc2 The bank added Russian corporates, which had been locked out of external debt market since the summer of 2008, are starting to take advantage of appetite for emerging market external debt although so far the issuance has been limited to top-tier names.\par \par \uc2 A prolonged period of low interest rates would mean liquidity needs a parking slot and support high-yielding emerging market debt for several quarters, but intermediate corrections were possible, it said.\par \par \uc2 "A potential trigger for a high-yield credit correction is the beginning of the tightening cycle in the major economies, which could reduce the attractiveness of high yielders," the bank said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, a favourable development in negotiations with the International Monetary Fund (IMF) continued to support the Turkish lira, which rose a third of a percent <TRY=> to 1.49 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The government, locked in negotiations with the IMF over a major loan deal since the previous stand-by expired in May 2008, said on Monday there was no discord with the IMF over the content of an economic programme.\par \par \uc2 Negotiations may produce a deal by October, when the IMF and the World Bank will hold their bi-annual meeting in Istanbul. (Additional reporting by Sebastian Tong; editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|HX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090828e58p000pp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
