\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Israel cbank buys  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  again after rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2009\par 10:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dealers estimate \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases up to $100 million\par \par \uc2 * More rate hikes expected this year\par \par \uc2 * Shekel advances 0.2 percent versus dollar\par \par \uc2 * Analysts see trend to stronger shekel\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds details, comments)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Aug 25 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel, trying to prevent a further appreciation of the shekel <ILS=> after its surprise rate rise, on Tuesday bought up to $100 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the shekel still gained versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 One dealer at \uc2 Israel Discount Bank\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $50 million to $70 million, while a Bank Leumi dealer said it was between $50 million and $100 million.\par \par \uc2 "It was not an aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said the Discount dealer.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its key short-term borrowing rate by a quarter-point to 0.75 percent [ID:nLO650919] and analysts believe more increases are in the offing.\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2 's Reinhard Cluse now sees a quarter-point hike a month that will bring the key rate to 1.75 percent by the end of 2009.\par \par \uc2 To prevent the shekel from advancing and further damaging exports, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  before and after the late afternoon rate hike.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the market planned to keep on testing the Bank of Israel's resolve since most analysts expect the shekel to appreciate more.\par \par \uc2 "The market is still trying to check the Bank of Israel's nerves in some sense. It is trying to see how persistent the Bank of Israel will be at current levels," the Discount dealer said. "It looks like the dollar wants to go down."\par \par \uc2 The shekel's official rate was set at 3.796 per dollar, up 0.2 percent from Monday's rate of 3.8040 before the rate hike.\par \par \uc2 After closing at 3.8142, the shekel edged higher from the start of Tuesday's trade, advancing to an intraday peak of 3.7870 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel, though, has shown in recent sessions it does not want the dollar to fall below the 3.80 level and started buying dollars, although the purchases this week have been far lower than those earlier in the month when the central bought some $2.5 billion after the exchange rate hit 3.74.\par \par \uc2 Analysts predict the shekel, though, will ultimately return to a level of 3.5 to 3.7 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "We remain optimistic about the chances for further shekel appreciation," Citi emerging markets economist David Lubin wrote in a client note.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the shekel to end this year close to 3.7 per dollar, with risks to the downside," he added.\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sach's Ahmet Akarli said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, aimed at stemming speculative shekel demand, was unsustainable as it would call into question the inflation targeting framework and push rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in opposite directions.\par \par \uc2 "We continue to believe therefore that the Bank of Israel will let go of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 , once external demand recovery becomes more visible," he wrote in a client note.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel earlier this month halted a more than one-year programme of buying $100 million a day in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although it said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on days of "unusual movements" in the market. (Editing by Jon Boyle)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-SHEKEL/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090825e58p000i2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
