\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Shekel weakens as Israel c.bank keeps buying  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2009\par 14:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Shekel weakens 0.6 percent vs dollar\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $300-$400 mln of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Fischer says \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases can't last forever\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds details, comments)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Aug 5 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel bought large amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a third straight day on Wednesday in an effort to weaken the shekel <ILS=> against the dollar, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Stanley Fischer said the purchases cannot go on forever.\par \par \uc2 The purchases pushed the shekel 0.6 percent weaker against the dollar to 3.889.\par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated the Bank of Israel bought between $300 million and $400 million to bring its total close to $1.5 billion since announcing on Monday it would buy more than its usual $100 million a day.\par \par \uc2 "They (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) have been buying randomly all day," said a dealer at a large Israeli bank. "A few tens of millions at a time."\par \par \uc2 It is difficult to know exactly how much \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being bought since the Bank of Israel scatters its purchases among a number of banks' dealing rooms.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought around $500 million on both Monday and Tuesday to weaken the shekel that had appreciated 12 percent versus the dollar since late April and worrying policymakers that exports would be damaged further.\par \par \uc2 So far, the move has been a success in weakening the shekel from a Dec. 19 peak of 3.74 shekels per dollar. It reached 3.866 on Tuesday and additional \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases on Wednesday sent the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday high of 3.96 shekels.\par \par \uc2 Selling emerged at that point, leading dealers to believe 3.96 is a new resistance level for the dollar with support at 3.85.\par \par \uc2 For more than a year, the Bank of Israel had been buying $100 million a day of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the dual purpose of boosting \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and limiting the shekel's appreciation. Exports have already been hurt by low global demand and a stronger shekel would make Israeli exports less competitive.\par \par \uc2 After the shekel had appreciated by 12 percent, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday said it would expand its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and buy more than $100 million a day "in the event of unusual movements in the exchange rate". [ID:nL379377]\par \par \uc2 Fischer defended the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in a meeting of parliament's finance committe on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "I sleep much better at night ... but it's clear, we cannot continue buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forever," Fischer said.\par \par \uc2 "Everyone understands that in the long run, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot stand up to the market and win," he said, echoing the sentiments of analysts the past few sessions.\par \par \uc2 Fischer said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policies of influencing the exchange rate has helped exports from being hurt more, enabling the economy to emerge from recession sooner.\par \par \uc2 In late trading after the setting of the official rate, the shekel stood at 3.9050 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The shekel also weakened 1.25 percent against the pound sterling and 0.9 percent versus the euro. (Editing by Richard Balmforth)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-SHEKEL/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090805e5850011j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
