\par\par \b \uc2 Israel shekel strength may end this yr -cenbank\b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2008\par 14:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Aug 6 (Reuters) - The Israeli shekel's <ILS=> strength against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to fade and the unit may even weaken this year, the Bank of Israel said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The basic and long-term pressure strengthening the shekel is expected to moderate, and it is even possible that there will be a turnaround during the course of the year," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its quarterly inflation report.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel cited a number of factors, including an expected narrowing of the current account surplus in Israel's balance of payments, as well as daily purchases of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and an outflow of capital by investors if the global financial crisis eases.\par \par \uc2 It noted, however, that the shekel's exchange rate over the next few months is still likely to experience a period of volatility.\par \par \uc2 The shekel, which stands at 3.53 per dollar, has appreciated about 8.5 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far in 2008 after a 10 percent gain in 2007.\par \par \uc2 But its year-to-date increase had reached more than 18 percent to a nearly 12-year peak of 3.20 last month, boosted by large foreign capital inflows, a weak dollar globally, rising Israeli short-term interest rates and a repatriation of money into shekel assets by Israeli investors.\par \par \uc2 In order to prevent a further shekel appreciation, which would hurt exporters, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In March, it began buying $25 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day, raising to $100 million a day a month ago.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its aim was to raise its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by some $10 billion.\par \par \uc2 The shekel has also appreciated against the euro this year.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 CENTRALBANK-ISRAEL/SHEKEL|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080806e486001gj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
