\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Bank of Israel ups daily  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  purchases, shekel dives\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2008\par 16:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with further shekel decline, stock market close)\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, July 10 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel said on Thursday it was raising the amount of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases to $100 million a day from $25 million, sending the shekel <ILS=> tumbling nearly 5 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a brief statement that the action was part of its plan to boost its reserves to $35-$40 billion, from more than $31 billion currently, and came after the shekel had surged in recent sessions to hit a nearly 12-year high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The decision to increase the pace of purchases was taken after examining the programme in light of current market conditions, and the cumulative and rapid change in the exchange rate of the shekel," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Israel will continue to review the programme from time to time to take into account changing market conditions," it added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on March 20 had embarked on what was then a two-year plan to boost its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by about $10 billion through the purchase of $25 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the move to quadruple that amount was probably due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's view that the original amount was insufficient to halt the shekel's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The shekel earlier in the session had risen to 3.2041 per dollar, its strongest level since October 1996 and brought gains in 2008 to some 17 percent. It had rallied the past four weeks from a low of 3.43.\par \par \uc2 After the announcement, the shekel slid and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the shekel's representative rate at 3.3140 to the dollar, 2.6 percent weaker than Wednesday's rate of 3.23.\par \par \uc2 But the shekel, which had been one of the world's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  the first half of the year, continued to slide after the setting of the official rate to stand around 3.36 per dollar at 1430 GMT for a 4.9 percent drop from its intraday peak.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think this will stop the appreciation of the shekel. But the shekel will appreciate at a slower pace," said Roderick Ngotho, an emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UBS.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Israel Governor Stanley Fischer has been under heavy pressure to deal with the shekel's strength since exporters have begun to get hit hard. A drop in exports, a key driver of growth, could threaten the overall Israeli economy, which has remained fairly robust.\par \par \uc2 In March, when the shekel had soared over a few days, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the first time in over a decade and bought $600 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fischer is opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the belief that market forces should prevail, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since despite speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would enter the market if the shekel rose too much.\par \par \uc2 Despite the daily \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, the shekel has continued to gain, supported by a solid economy and Bank of Israel short-term interest rate increases aimed at curbing inflation pressures.\par \par \uc2 A third straight quarter-point rate increase is expected on July 28, a move that would bring the key rate to 4 percent.\par \par \uc2 Benchmark 10-year bond prices <ILSAHR2683=TA> shed 0.4 percent to push its yield to 5.93 percent from 5.86 percent, while key Tel Aviv share indexes closed 0.6 percent lower.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 CENTRALBANK-ISRAEL/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|BNX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080710e47a000xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
