\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Israel shekel jumps to new 11-1/2-yr high vs dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 642 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2008\par 14:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with further shekel gain, closing share indexes, analyst comment)\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, May 29 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel <ILS=> strengthened another 0.8 percent against the dollar in heavy trading on Thursday, boosted by heavy corporate selling of dollars.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel set its official daily rate at 3.2620 shekels per dollar, its strongest level since January 14, 1997 from Wednesday's rate of 3.2880.\par \par \uc2 The shekel gained another 0.7 percent after the setting of the official rate to stand at 3.2380 to the dollar at 1450 GMT.\par \par \uc2 Dollar-shekel opened at 3.29 and remained steady until around 2 pm local time (1100 GMT), when selling intensified.\par \par \uc2 Companies typically sell dollars and buy shekels on the last few days of the months to pay salaries. But dealers said activity on Thursday was heavier than usual.\par \par \uc2 "All the companies who needed to sell dollars kept waiting for the dollar to go up. But that didn't happen," said a dealer at \uc2 Israel Discount Bank.\uc2  "Today we saw big volumes of dollar selling."\par \par \uc2 So far in 2008, the shekel has appreciated about 18 percent against the dollar, making it among the best performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That follows a 10 percent gain in 2007.\par \par \uc2 Part of the rise has come because of the globally weak dollar but lately, dollar-shekel has tended to decouple from euro-dollar.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the Bank of Israel raised its key lending rate a quarter-point to 3.50 percent to widen the differential between Israeli and U.S. rates to 1.25 points.\par \par \uc2 With inflation soaring to an annual 4.7 percent in April from 3.7 percent in March, analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reverse all the 100 basis points of easing earlier in the year.\par \par \uc2 RATES, \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 "We expect the shekel to remain well supported in the period ahead," \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  analysts wrote in a report on Thursday. "At this stage, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have shifted its focus back onto inflation and appears less concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.\par \par \uc2 "Overall, monetary policy action will remain the key driver of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the next few weeks, in our view," it added.\par \par \uc2 When the dollar fell sharply to 3.35 in mid-March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $600 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide. It was the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in more than a decade and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Stanley Fischer made it clear \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not occur often.\par \par \uc2 The move pushed the dollar back to 3.65 in April.\par \par \uc2 Still, as the rate moved back to 3.35 shekels and below in recent days, the market expected another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since a strong shekel tends to make Israeli exports less attractive and would hurt economic growth. It also helps to offset some inflation pressures since 40 percent of housing rental costs are quoted in dollars but paid in shekels.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the levels the market expected them to. The market in general thought 3.33-3.34 was a line in the sand for the Bank of Israel," said Nandita Singh, an emerging markets strategist at \uc2 JPMorgan Chase.\par \par \uc2 "When they didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that emboldened investors to sell dollar-shekel," she said, adding that along with rate hikes, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could now potentially use a stronger shekel to fight inflation.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the shekel jumped 1.6 percent to 5.0736.\par \par \uc2 Tel Aviv share indexes closed 0.9 percent higher, while the benchmark 10-year bond's price <ILSAHR2683=TA> edged up 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Gerrard Raven)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ISRAEL/SHEKEL (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|MD|E|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080529e45t00101\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
