\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar up 4 pct vs shekel as Israel c.bank buys  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 12:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, March 24 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel <ILS=> weakened nearly 4 percent against the dollar on Monday ahead of an interest rate decision and as the Bank of Israel embarked on a plan to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The shekel was at 3.53 per dollar at 1100 GMT, compared with Thursday's official rate of 3.3990. There was no official rate set on Friday due to holidays.   \par \par \uc2 Late on Thursday, the dollar began to strengthen after the Bank of Israel announced that starting on March 24, it would buy $25 million a day of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for two years in an attempt to raise its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by up to $10 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 "I am not sure it was the full ($25 million) amount but it was some of it at least," said a dealer at  \uc2 Israel Discount Bank.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the markets on March 13 by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market after it saw the dollar slide by some 6 percent against the shekel in just a few days to a low of 3.35 shekels. It said it sought to stabilise the market with its first foray into the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in more than a decade.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears that a strong shekel will make Israeli exports less attractive, and combined with a global slowdown, hurt Israel's economy.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar had shed 10 percent against the shekel in 2007 and had lost as much as 14 percent until last week. (Reporting by Steven Scheer)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ISRAEL-SHEKEL|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080324e43o000j5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
