\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Bank of Israel to raise  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves by $10 bln   \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 14:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, comments)   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, March 20 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel said on Thursday it would implement a plan to increase its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by buying about $10 billion over the next two years.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement that starting on March 24 it will buy about $25 million a day.   \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Israel explains that after an extensive study conducted by the bank over the past few months, it decided to raise its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to a level of $35 billion to $40 billion from $28 billion currently," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 "This is in light of the economy's needs and on the backdrop of rapid growth of the economy in the past few years and its increasingly becoming part of the global economy and the global financial system."   \par \par \uc2 Last week, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in more than a decade, buying an estimated $500 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt a rapid slide in the dollar against the shekel <ILS=>.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the sum it plans to buy is only a fraction of the daily trading volumes in the local market, which averages about $2 billion a day.   \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Israel will re-examine this programme from time to time, taking into consideration the changing market conditions," it said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 It noted that purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be made in a manner that would prevent unwanted consequences on the shekel's exchange rate development.   \par \par \uc2 Current conditions in the market enable the bank to increase its reserves in a manner that is consistent with its interest rate policy while strengthening the stability of the financial system and the economy, the bank said.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel said the new plan does not change its focus on its main targets -- preserving price stability while taking into consideration economic growth and employment. (Reporting by Steven Scheer and Tova Cohen; Editing by Ron Askew)   \par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-CENBANK/RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080320e43k000wl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
