\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Shekel seen rising despite cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  cloud\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 16:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, March 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shekel <ILS=> is poised to extend its 11-year high versus the dollar in the near term, even under the threat the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may again buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem its strength.\par \par \uc2 With the globally weak dollar tumbling to new lows versus the shekel last week -- the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed its hands-off policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, saying it would not rule out further \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases.\par \par \uc2 It bought an estimated $500 million worth of dollars last Thursday and Friday, a move that stopped the dollar's freefall against the shekel but did not stop it from weakening further.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot change the direction of the market," said Leonor Terkieltaub, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department at the IBI brokerage in Tel Aviv.\par \par \uc2 Analysts are split as to whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late 1997 was necessary. But most believe that without it the dollar would be weaker than its current 3.3750 shekels -- its lowest level since April 1997.\par \par \uc2 Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar, which initially moved to 3.47 from 3.35 shekels, has resumed a year-long weakening trend.\par \par \uc2 "Higher (dollar) levels will be used to sell dollars again," said Terkeiltaub.\par \par \uc2 In the days before the action, the dollar slid from 3.60 shekels to 3.35 to prompt the extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move.\par \par \uc2 "The main issue right now is not dollar-shekel. It's the dollar around the world," said Ittai Ben-Zeev, head of sales and trading at Bank Leumi. "For the dollar to rise against the shekel you need it to rise around the world."\par \par \uc2 But that seems unlikely with U.S. interest rates falling, worries over the U.S. financial sector persisting, and the euro <EUR=> near a record high at $1.57.\par \par \uc2 Ben-Zeev said the dollar seemed to be holding above a key support level of 3.35 shekels for now. Should that break, "it could easily be at 3.20," he added.\par \par \uc2 EXPORTS HURT\par \par \uc2 The shekel has been one of the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past year, boosted by a robust economy, strong foreign investment, higher interest rates in Israel than the United States and the weak global dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Although it may seem unwise to bet against a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  determined to sell its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we doubt the Bank of Israel will ultimately succeed in weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  wrote in a report.\par \par \uc2 "There are very strong fundamental reasons for the shekel to strengthen," it said, citing the widening Israeli-U.S. rate differential, the shekel being attractive on a trade-weighted basis, a strong economy and Israelis moving capital back to Israel. "We would look to add on shekel weakness."\par \par \uc2 The shekel rose 10 percent versus the dollar in 2007 and is up another 13 percent this year. The gains worry policymakers since exporters' troubles threaten to hurt the economy.\par \par \uc2 It remains unclear whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  succeeded, despite signalling that Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Stanley Fischer would not allow violent moves in the market.\par \par \uc2 "People who have real hedging to do need to do it regardless of what he (Fischer) is doing in the market and not be reliant on him coming to buy dollars," said Neil Corney, treasurer of \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's Israel office.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think it necessarily changes the rules of trading."\par \par \uc2 But Ben-Zeev said volatility in the market has now reached 22 percent from 12 percent a month ago and 5 percent last year.\par \par \uc2 "We now have a new player who entered the game after sitting 11 years on the bench," he said. (Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-SHEKEL/ (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080319e43j00151\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
