\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Israel shekel up 1.3 pct to 11-yr peak vs dollar   \b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 15:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds official rates, dealer comments)   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, March 18 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel <ILS=> strengthened another 1.3 percent against the dollar to hit a fresh 11-year high, as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  held near a record low versus the euro ahead of an expected Federal Reserve rate cut.   \par \par \uc2 The shekel's official rate was set at 3.38 per dollar -- its strongest level since April 4, 1997 -- compared with Monday's rate of 3.4260.   \par \par \uc2 Over the past two sessions since the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market late last week, the shekel has appreciated 2.7 percent. It is up 13 percent so far in 2008 after a 10 percent gain in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said activity was thin throughout the day, when the dollar-shekel traded between a rate of 3.38 and 3.41.   \par \par \uc2 "We saw some dollar sellers in the market. Euro/dollar is up. The market is thin and players are defensive," said a dealer at a foreign bank in Tel Aviv.   \par \par \uc2 He noted that the market has stabilised since the Bank of Israel last Thursday and Friday bought an estimated $500 million to stem a rapid slide in the dollar to 3.35 from 3.60 last week.   \par \par \uc2 "If he didn't pump half a billion dollars into the market, we would probably be trading at 3.20 by now," the dealer said, referring to Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Stanley Fischer's market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "He didn't stop the trend but he managed to stop the freefall. He balanced the market."   \par \par \uc2 Fischer, a staunch opponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , this week said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first foray into the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in more than a decade was meant to stabilise the market. He stressed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  every day and that he was not trying to target any specific dollar-shekel level.   \par \par \uc2 Later on Tuesday, the Fed is expected to slash U.S. rates by as much as one percentage point. That kept the dollar near a record low at $1.58 per euro.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer is expected to follow suit with a cut next Monday of a half-point.   \par \par \uc2 Tel Aviv shares gained 1.8 percent <.TA25> <.TA100> and benchmark bond prices <ILSAHR2683=TA> slipped 0.1 percent to push the yield to 5.40 percent from 5.38 percent on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Against the euro the shekel <EURILS=> gained to 5.3370 from 5.4013 on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 On the crosses, the shekel traded up 2.3 percent at 3.4555 per 100 yen and 0.7 percent higher against the pound at 6.8234.   \par \par \uc2 For further information double click on the following:   \par \par \uc2 <ILS=> for latest commercial bank shekel/dollar rates.   \par \par \uc2 <ILS1=> for a list of commercial bank shekel/dollar rates.   \par \par \uc2 <ILS2=> for a list of commercial bank shekel/basket rates.   \par \par \uc2 <BOIT12> for Bank of Israel rates.   \par \par \uc2 <FXIL> for Israeli spot and mid rates by the hour.   \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Steven Scheer)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ISRAEL-SHEKEL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080318e43i0014o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
