\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-UPDATE 1-'Herd' behaviour led Israel c.bank to act-Fischer   \b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 15:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Refiles to fix typo in paragraph 12)   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, background)   \par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer and Avida Landau   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, March 16 (Reuters) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Stanley Fischer on Sunday defended a rare \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and stressed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want to make a habit of buying dollars.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel bought an undisclosed amount of dollars on Thursday and Friday following a 6 percent drop in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the shekel throughout the week. It was the first \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late 1997.   \par \par \uc2 "We concluded that we saw a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that is not anchored well and began seeing herd behaviour," Fischer told a news conference. "On the basis of this we decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to bring stability to the market."   \par \par \uc2 Although the dollar-shekel was weak all year, it had not moved as sharply as it did last week when it went from 3.60 per dollar early last Monday 3.35 on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Once the exchange rate fell below 3.40, the Bank of Israel stepped in and bought dollars. At first it didn't work and required another round on Thursday and then a third on Friday morning.   \par \par \uc2 "Initially the action was successful. The weakening of the dollar was stopped," Fischer said. "The dollar got stronger and the shekel got weaker."   \par \par \uc2 The dollar jumped from an 11-year low of 3.35 shekels to a level of 3.4740 by Friday afternoon.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer rejected the notion that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was targeting a certain dollar-shekel rate.   \par \par \uc2 Trading in Israel's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will resume on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer declined to say how much the Bank of Israel bought but Israeli media and banks estimated the total at around $500 million.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer has been a staunch opponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets but he said that last week's freefall of the dollar against the shekel <ILS=> could no longer be ignored.   \par \par \uc2 "We have no intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a daily basis," he said. "We will continue to trust the activities of the market except for extraordinary occurrences like we saw. We hope this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be rare."   \par \par \uc2 He said that despite the action, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main mandate of keeping inflation low had not changed.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer declined to comment when asked whether he would lower short-term interest rates again at the end of the month as another way to weaken the shekel. In a surprise move, he lowered Israel's key lending rate by a half-point to 3.75 on Feb. 25.   \par \par \uc2 But the rate cut failed to halt a rally in the shekel against the dollar that has reached about 11 percent since the beginning of the year on top of a 10 percent appreciation in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer noted that in the long-term, he expected the shekel to continue to appreciating against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 (Editing by Jason Neely)   \par \par \uc2 SHEKEL-CENBANK/FISCHER  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|MD|RNP|DNP   \par \par