\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  calls news conference on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 10:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TEL AVIV, March 16 (Reuters) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Stanley Fischer will meet journalists on Sunday afternoon to discuss the latest developments in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading and explain the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent actions.   \par \par \uc2 On Friday the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for a second straight session, buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to cool the shekel's <ILS=> rally.   \par \par \uc2 With the shekel appreciating 6 percent against the dollar in the first four days of trade last week and hitting a nearly 11-year high on Thursday, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was compelled to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the first time since 1997.   \par \par \uc2 It bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Friday, sending the shekel's official rate down 2.1 percent against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer had long rejected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, saying he prefers to let market forces prevail.   \par \par \uc2 Israel's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is closed on Sunday.   \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tova Cohen; Editing by Jason Neely)   \par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-CENBANK/|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080316e43g0005w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley