\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Shekel slides 2 pct vs dlr after c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 718 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 12:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, comments)   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, March 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shekel <ILS=> slid 2.1 percent on Friday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for a second straight session.   \par \par \uc2 The shekel's official rate was set at 3.4740 per dollar, compared with Thursday's rate of 3.4030, its strongest since June 10, 1997.   \par \par \uc2 The shekel has appreciated some 6 percent against the dollar from Monday to Thursday and the Bank of Israel said it was compelled to act and break its more than decade-long policy of staying out of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 "In light of the unusual action of the exchange rate of the shekel the last few days the Bank of Israel bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during trade," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in statements on Thursday and on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 It declined to provide any further information.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers at Israeli banks said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $200 million in two waves on Thursday and another $50 million on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to change the trend of shekel strength because the strength of the shekel is partially caused by dollar weakness, and aggressive policy easing by the Federal Reserve, which is beyond the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's control (and) the fundamentals for shekel strength are strong, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still reasonably weak on a real trade weighted basis,"  \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  wrote in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 It added that local investors may start to regain a "home bias" given the relative calm at home, and the turbulence in markets outside Israel.   \par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Stanley Fischer has long rejected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, saying he prefers to let market forces prevail.   \par \par \uc2 FIRST \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  IN 10 YEARS   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since late 1997.   \par \par \uc2 "The question is: what is the reason?," said a dealer at an Israeli bank. "Do they just want to stop the dollar from going down or do they want the dollar to go up?"   \par \par \uc2 The shekel's strength has been a sore spot for Fischer, who has come under pressure from exporters to act as Israel's strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hurt exports and threatened economic growth.   \par \par \uc2 In an attempt to stem the shekel's rally this year, against the euro and other key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as the dollar, Fischer lowered short-term interest rates by a surprising half-point to 3.75 on Feb. 25.   \par \par \uc2 But the rate cut failed to dent the shekel, which on Thursday extended gains to 13 percent against the dollar so far in 2008 after a 10 percent appreciation in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  first bought \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the dollar had reached 3.40 shekels on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 At the same time Moody's Investors Service said it was placing Israel's A2 government bond ratings and A2 country ceiling on review for a possible upgrade.   \par \par \uc2 That sent the dollar down to 3.35 shekels, prompting a more aggressive action of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying. It appeared to work since the dollar rose back to around 3.44.   \par \par \uc2 Friday's action then moved the exhange rate back to 3.47.   \par \par \uc2 After the setting of the official rate the shekel edged back to 3.4630 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Against the euro the shekel <EURILS=> shed 2.2 percent to 5.4106 from 5.2949 on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 On the crosses, the shekel traded down 2.2 percent at 3.4529 per 100 yen and 1.8 percent lower against the pound at 7.0493.   \par \par \uc2 The market is awaiting the release of February inflation data at 1200 GMT for clues on future interest rate changes. It is seen down 0.3 percent on the month and up 3.5 percent year on year.   \par \par \uc2 Israeli stocks and bonds do not trade on Fridays.   \par \par \uc2 For further information double click on the following:   \par \par \uc2 <ILS=> for latest commercial bank shekel/dollar rates.   \par \par \uc2 <ILS1=> for a list of commercial bank shekel/dollar rates.   \par \par \uc2 <ILS2=> for a list of commercial bank shekel/basket rates.   \par \par \uc2 <BOIT12> for Bank of Israel rates.   \par \par \uc2 <FXIL> for Israeli spot and mid rates by the hour.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ISRAEL-SHEKEL/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|MD|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080314e43e001cw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
