\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2 's Fischer:Sees No Need To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  -BIS   \b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2007\par 10:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with additional comments on the Israeli economy and developments in global markets)   \par \par \uc2 By Natasha Brereton   \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \uc2 BASEL (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to adjust the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its governor said Sunday.   \par \par \uc2 "The shekel has undergone a correction in the last few weeks, so I think the market seems to be taking care of any concerns over its valuation," Stanley Fischer told reporters on the sidelines of meetings at the Bank for International Settlements in Basel.   \par \par \uc2 With regards to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Fischer said he saw "no need to do that, no desire to do that, no likelihood of its being done."   \par \par \uc2 The shekel has appreciated 4.78% against the dollar since the beginning of 2007, and 10.57% in the last year, the Bank of Israel said earlier this month.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer said that most recent data show that Israeli economic growth "is doing very well."   \par \par \uc2 The nation's gross domestic product grew at an annual rate of 6.3% in the first quarter of 2007, up from an annual expansion of 5.7% in the first quarter of 2006.   \par \par \uc2 "The indicator for May came in indicating growth in the current region of around 5%, perhaps a bit more," he said.   \par \par \uc2 There is "low inflation (and a) strong balance of payments, so all that looks fine," although of course "you have to stay on your guard," he added.   \par \par \uc2 The Israeli consumer price index was flat on the month in May and fell 1.3% on the year - well below the government target range for annual inflation of between 1% and 3%.   \par \par \uc2 Israeli interest rates currently stand at 3.5%. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut the policy rate seven times in the past eight months, in an effort to bring annual inflation into the government's target range.   \par \par \uc2 The governor also expressed the view that a recent rise in global bond yields shouldn't have a significant negative effect on Israel or on other emerging market economies.   \par \par \uc2 "As for the interest rate correction, I think the economy is in reasonably good shape, which means for most the emerging market countries we're not going to see that having any major impact," Fischer said.   \par \par \uc2 "It may slow down a bit the capital inflows, but they have been taking place at such a rapid rate that a little slowdown isn't going to make a very big difference."   \par \par \uc2 -By Natasha Brereton, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 20 7842 9254; natasha.brereton@dowjones.com [ 24-06-07 0845GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070624e36o0001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
