\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Israel shekel jumps 1 pct to match late-2000 high   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer and Sergio Tjong-Alvares   \par \uc2 731 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2007\par 11:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comments, official rates)   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, April 12 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel <ILS=> jumped 1 percent versus a globally weak dollar on Thursday to reach its highest level since late 2000, boosted further by sentiment that there was little to halt the shekel's rally.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that with the dollar weak around the world and \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief voicing opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- buying dollars -- to halt the shekel's surge, the shekel would probably appreciate further.   \par \par \uc2 The shekel's official rate was set at 4.0660 per dollar -- its strongest level since December 29, 2000 -- from 4.1070 per dollar on Wednesday. It hit a high of 4.0575 during the day.   \par \par \uc2 In late trading, after the setting of the official rate, the shekel was steady at 4.0590 to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Israel's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rallied from 4.20 to the dollar on March 26 and from 4.13 in the last four trading sessions.   \par \par \uc2 Since the beginning of the year, the shekel is up 4 percent against the dollar after appreciating eight percent in 2006.   \par \par \uc2 The latest spike in the shekel came Wednesday after Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Stanley Fischer said he had no intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on grounds it could destabilise the market and turn investors' main focus away from the economy.   \par \par \uc2 "People took that as a sign the shekel can strengthen further," Citicorp's Neil Corney said.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer is under heavy pressure to either reduce rates sharply or buy dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to try and weaken the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the robust shekel has not only led to disinflation but also economic hardship for local exporters.   \par \par \uc2 The shekel had begun to rally in late March Fischer left short-term lending rates unchanged after five straight monthly interest rate reductions totalling 1.5 percentage points.   \par \par \uc2 The cuts were aimed at stemming the rise in the shekel -- which had been at 4.70 to the dollar a year ago -- which led to a rapid disinflation trend that brought inflation to below zero and outside of the official annual inflation target range of between 1 and 3 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Helping the shekel were continued foreign capital inflows and the dollar's weakness against the euro and many emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , both of which have more than offset interest rate cuts.   \par \par \uc2 "If you look at the world dollar, you can also see there is quite a lot of strength for all \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar," Corney said. "The other thing that is happening is we are seeing continuing investments into Israel -- both portfolio and real investments -- and that is fueling shekel strength."   \par \par \uc2 Fischer now may have no choice to lower rates again but he told a news conference on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in a difficult position since the economy was growing very fast and prices not linked to the dollar were rising.   \par \par \uc2 Housing and many imported goods are linked to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , comprising 29 percent of the consumer price index.   \par \par \uc2 Still, some analysts noted that though the dollar is globally weaker, the shekel remained undervalued against the dollar as well as the euro and pound.   \par \par \uc2 "Around 45 percent of Israeli exports are actually destined for Europe and the UK, and that the shekel is not particularly strong versus the pound or euro,"  \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2  analyst Lucy Bethell said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 "With local price pressures likely to build on past rate cuts, the Bank should highlight this fact."   \par \par \uc2 The basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , composed of the dollar, euro, sterling and yen, was fixed at 4.6692 compared with 4.7133 on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 On the crosses, the shekel traded at 3.4064 per 100 yen compared with 3.4449, against the euro at 5.4730 from 5.5118 shekels, and against the pound at 8.0381 from 8.1210.   \par \par \uc2 For further information double click on the following:   \par \par \uc2 <ILS=> for latest commercial bank shekel/dollar rates.   \par \par \uc2 <ILS1=> for a list of commercial bank shekel/dollar rates.   \par \par \uc2 <ILS2=> for a list of commercial bank shekel/basket rates.   \par \par \uc2 <BOIJ> for Bank of Israel rates.   \par \par \uc2 <FXIL> for Israeli spot and mid rates by the hour.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ISRAEL-SHEKEL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070412e34c000ri\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
