\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  c.bank head says against  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2007\par 12:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds further quotes, shekel reaction)   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, April 11 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the shekel's <ILS=> appreciation, and such a drastic policy move could destabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Governor Stanley Fischer said on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "We have no intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  or entering the market," Fischer told a news conference, adding:"It will change the nature of the market completely."   \par \par \uc2 Helped by record foreign investment, the shekel has surged to a more than six-year high against the dollar, prompting calls from analysts for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars since a string of short-term interest rate reductions have so far failed to stem the shekel's rise and the disinflation trend.   \par \par \uc2 After an 8 percent appreciation in 2006, the shekel has added another 3 percent so far in 2007 versus the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "If we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , people will be expecting it," Fischer said, noting he prefers that the market continue to focus mostly on economic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer acknowleged that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has no tradition of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence the shekel's value, was in a difficult position regarding its interest rate policy because inflation remains below zero while the economy was growing fast.   \par \par \uc2 He said the interest rate was the sole tool the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to try and maintain price stability, defined in Israel as an annual inflation rate of between 1 and 3 percent.   \par \par \uc2 In an attempt to bring inflation back to within the official target range, Fischer lowered the bank's key lending rate five straight rate times from October through February to 4 percent from 5.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 A belief that the economy was growing fast enough to return inflation to within the target later this year led Fischer to keep rates unchanged in late March. More cuts seemed unlikely.   \par \par \uc2 But with the shekel gaining further on the dollar -- advancing to 4.1060, its strongest level since February 2001 -- expectations have grown in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that Fischer has no choice but to resume rate cuts later in April. Some economists believe a reduction of a half-point is possible.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer declined to say whether he would consider another rate reduction on April 22, the next scheduled policy decision.   \par \par \uc2 "ECONOMY GROWING SO FAST"   \par \par \uc2 "We are in a situation where we have to consider how rapidly we lower the interest rate or at all because the economy is growing so fast," Fischer said.   \par \par \uc2 He cited a contraction in the output gap that indicates "the economy is on the move".   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel forecasts economic growth of 5.1 percent in 2007, which would be the fourth year in a row of growth around 5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "The economy is in a good situation," Fischer said.   \par \par \uc2 He noted that some of what was happening in the economy and to the exchange rate was not under his control.   \par \par \uc2 "The problem is the dollar is falling all over the world," Fischer said, owing mainly to the large U.S. current account deficit. Israel has a current account surplus.   \par \par \uc2 With housing and many imported goods linked to the dollar, those costs have an immediate impact on inflation in Israel. Data show that while the overall consumer price index in February stood 0.8 percent lower than the prior 12 months, the CPI was up 0.4 percent excluding housing.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer said he would prefer to target "core" inflation, which removes much of the dollar/shekel's influence like in the United States but he doubted the Israeli public would accept it.   \par \par \uc2 "Domestic prices are rising and only imports and housing are falling," he said. "But negative inflation is not a problem.   \par \par \uc2 "We have decided to focus on the index that people understand -- the CPI -- and if we don't hit the target we try and explain it and that's what is happening today," he added.   \par \par \uc2 Fischer also said that while the economy was doing well and government was adhering to responsible budget policies, more needs to be done on reducing Israel's huge public sector debt, which is about 88 percent of gross domestic product.   \par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-FISCHER/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|BNX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070411e34b000qf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
