\par\par \b \uc2 Lebanon says  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves enough to support pound  \b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2006\par 15:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BEIRUT, July 15 (Reuters) - Lebanon's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Saturday the bank has enough foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend the Lebanese pound exchange rate and meet the financial markets' needs despite Israel's military offensive.  \par \par \uc2 "We have around $13 billion of foreign reserves and given the situation we are living in the financial markets have not reacted that negatively because they know the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's capabilities," Riad Salameh told Voice of Lebanon radio.  \par \par \uc2 The Lebanese pound <LBP=> has been trading at the weakest end of its official 1,501-1,514 band. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to offer dollars after \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  intensified its military campaign against Lebanon after Hizbollah guerrillas captured two Israeli soldiers on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue its policy to support the pound and offer liquidity with the current interest rates," Salameh said.  \par \par \uc2 The Stock Exchange also temporarily cut the daily limits set on price moves for listed securities and bonds to five percent from 10 percent on Friday for a week to bolster the markets after the military confrontation shook confidence.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark BLOM Stock Index <.BLSI> fell 3.14 percent on Friday, for a tumble of just under 14 percent over the week.  \par \par \uc2 MIDEAST-ECONOMY-LEBANON|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|MD|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060715e27f000j1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw