\par\par \b \uc2  Israel shekel sinks as cease-fire seen shaky. \b0\par\par\uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2003\par 16:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, July 8 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel  slid 1.2 percent against the dollar on Tuesday after a Palestinian suicide bombing threatened a 10-day cease-fire that may have signalled an end a strong shekel rally, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel's representative, or official, rate was set at 4.3340, from Monday's rate of 4.2830 to the dollar - its strongest level since December 20, 2001. \par \par \uc2  After the setting of the rate, the shekel sank further to close to 4.37 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Things were looking good up until today," said a dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. "After we saw that the bomb was a terrorist attack and not a mistake fear has emerged that the cease-fire may fail." \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Tuesday, a West Bank-based cell of the Islamic Jihad militant group took responsibility for a suicide bombing on Monday night that killed a woman in Israel. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that suicide bombings have not impacted the market much in recent months because they had been so frequent. \par \par \uc2  "But now, things are starting to get better so any terrorist attack makes the market think we may be going back" to when they occurred more often, the Mizrahi dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He noted that foreign banks were the big dollar buyers today. \par \par \uc2  "They made profits on the (dollar's) way down so it was a good time to close," he said. "There was a bit of foreign banks closing short postions in fear the bomb may cause a new crisis in the cease-fire." \par \par \uc2  The shekel had jumped some 10 percent against the dollar in the past few month, buoyed by progress on Middle East peace, tighter fiscal policies and a wide interest rate gap between Israel and the United States. \par \par \uc2  In recent days, some dealers said the shekel could still gain further to 4.25 or more because Israel's key lending rate stands at 7.5 percent to the U.S. federal funds rate of 1 percent but Tuesday's move may have shown the shekel was still vulnerable. \par \par \uc2  "This might have been the trigger to closing short positions," said the dealer. \par \par \uc2  Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lowered its key rate from 9.1 percent in recent months, dealers said the 6.5-point gap over the U.S.'s fed funds rate makes holding dollars difficult. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Ariel Sharon and Finance Minister Benjamin Netanyahu have urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower rates faster in the wake of zero inflation and the stronger shekel's impact on exports, but Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor has said he has no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market or drop rates sharply to weaken the shekel. \par \par \uc2  He stood firm on his policy to steer clear from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the strengthening shekel, saying only the market should determine the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  The basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , composed of the dollar, euro, pound sterling and yen, was fixed at 4.7116 shekels against 4.6638 shekels on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded at 3.6606 shekels per 100 yen compared with 3.6278, against the euro at 4.9018 shekels from 4.8633 and against the pound at 7.0993 versus 7.0618. \par \par \uc2  (For further information \par \par \uc2   . \par \par \uc2    for a list of commercial bank shekel/dollar rates. \par \par \uc2   . \par \par \uc2   . \par \par \uc2    ). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030708dz7800r65\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
