\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  c.bank says won't  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2003\par 14:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, July 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief on Thursday stood firm on his policy to steer clear from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the strengthening shekel, saying only the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should determine the shekel's rate. \par \par \uc2  The shekel has jumped some 10 percent against the dollar in the past few months, prompting calls for lower short-term interest rates or direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from curtailing exports and damaging \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recession-hit economy further. \par \par \uc2  "Attempts to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading to guide the exchange rate will fail and is an idea that is playing with fire," Bank of Israel Governor David Klein told an economic conference. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks, Finance Ministry officials and those depending on exports have said the shekel - which on Thursday was at a fresh 18-month high at 4.29 to the dollar - was too strong and could hurt the economy, which has been in recession for more than 2-1/2 years due to a global slowdown and bloody Israeli-Palestinian conflict. \par \par \uc2  "There is no basis for arguing the shekel is either too strong or too weak," Klein said. "This is a market rate." \par \par \uc2  He reiterated his position that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually fails since "you are working against the market" while "interest rates are not a tool for controlling the exchange rate". \par \par \uc2  The shekel has gained on expectations of tighter fiscal policies, the end to the Iraq war in which Israel was unscathed amd optimism over the start of a process that could lead to a peace deal with the Palestinians. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030703dz7300nb8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
