\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  cbank denies reports of  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 13:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, March 10 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday denied media reports that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading on Friday to prevent banks from artificially boosting the exchange rate ahead of a dollar-linked bond redemption. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it called banks as part of its management of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing to check on the difference between quote prices and rates at which transactions were taking place. \par \par \uc2  "It would be an exaggeration to call it an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman. "It was simply part of our ongoing activities and happens from time to time." \par \par \uc2  Israeli media reports on Monday said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading to prevent manipulation of the exchange rate ahead of Friday's redemption of 3.6 billion shekels ($742 million) of bonds. Payment to bondholders was based on Friday's representative, or official, rate which was set at 4.8490 shekels to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose against the shekel last week as institutional investors tried to prop up the dollar's rate against the shekel ahead of the bond expiration. \par \par \uc2  The Ha'aretz daily said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it noticed the banks were offering quotes that were not in line with transaction prices. The paper said the banks were trading the dollar at 4.84 shekels but quoting it at 4.86 shekels and that foreign banks had complained that Israeli banks were manipulating the rate. \par \par \uc2  The bond holders were mostly institutional investors, including banks, which had an interest in seeing a high rate set ahead of the redemption, Ha'aretz said. \par \par \uc2  "I would not call this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  calls the banks from time to time to check the level of the market," said a dealer from a major bank who requested anonymity. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at another of Israel's largest banks said the banks had an interest in the official rate being set as high as possible but said the gap between the quote and transaction prices was less than cited in media reports. \par \par \uc2  "The bank called and asked us to check the price difference," the dealer said. "That happens sometimes, particularly when trading is volatile. It doesn't happen every day, but it's not rare either." \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 4.85 shekels). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030310dz3a00phc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
