\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rand strength ebbs, shekel down after bomb. \b0\par\par\uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2002\par 12:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 8 (Reuters) - The South African rand eased off five month highs against the dollar on Wednesday after earlier exporter buying had helped it extend its six-day old bull run. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the shekel dropped back to its weakest levels in over a week against the dollar in the wake of another suicide bomb attack in \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the zloty pulled back after verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Polish Finance Minister. \par \par \uc2  The rand found upward momentum initially from exporter demand, but ran out of steam ahead of the key 10 level. However, analysts think that level will come under pressure again in coming sessions. \par \par \uc2  "The rand has risen on a combination of flows and fundamentals," said Callum Henderson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  "Last year we had a loose monetary policy, and a relatively tight fiscal policy, but the mix has changed to tighter monetary policy, with a looser fiscal stance this year, and the rand has risen on that basis," said Henderson. \par \par \uc2  Firm commodity prices and the prospect of another rate hike from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June have underpinned the rand's recent rally. \par \par \uc2  South African Reserve Bank Governor further bolstered expectations of another rate hike in June on Tuesday, saying that inflation was on an upward trend. \par \par \uc2  "If it (inflation) is on the upside the Reserve Bank has one instrument...which is to use its monetary policy stance," said Mboweni. \par \par \uc2  The recent rise in bullion prices to their highest levels in over two-year have added to the rand's bull run. South Africa is the world's largest gold producer. \par \par \uc2  The market has also broken through some key technical levels, with the 200-day moving average around 10.3140 giving way on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At 0930 GMT, the rand traded at 10.1587 to the dollar from 10.17 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  BOMB ATTACK HITS SHEKEL \par \par \uc2  The latest suicide bomb attack in Israel left 15 dead and prompted Prime Minister Ariel Sharon to cut short his trip to the U.S. He also vowed to "hit back hard" against Palestinian militants. \par \par \uc2  Fresh security worries undermined the shekel, which retreated close to its recent record lows against the dollar below 4.90. \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded at 4.9050 to the dollar from 4.8620. \par \par \uc2  The zloty retreated from its recent highs as Finance Minister Marek Belka intensified his efforts to talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. \par \par \uc2  Belka said the strong zloty was a curse and called on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help take action to weaken it. He added that he was concerned over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's misguided monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that Belka's desire for a weaker zloty was well documented, but some also noted that the zloty had risen a long way in recent days and could be ripe for a pullback. \par \par \uc2  "Belka has said before that he sees fair value for the zloty around 4.25 to the dollar, so this is not a great surprise," said Simon Watts, emerging markets analyst at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  "Locals have been worried that non-residents might start pulling out of the bond market after recent signals from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the pace of monetary easing will slow, but you still get paid handsomely for taking on zloty risk," said Watts. \par \par \uc2  With benchmark interest rates at 9.5 percent, Poland still attracts investors in search of high yields. \par \par \uc2  The zloty traded at 3.6287 to the euro from 3.6197 and at 3.9839 to the dollar from 3.9642. \par \par \uc2  The Turkish lira climbed off recent lows against the dollar, finding support from news of strong Turkish industrial output in March. \par \par \uc2  Output rose 18.7 percent on the year, far in excess of the 4.3 percent predicted in a Reuters poll of analysts. \par \par \uc2  The lira traded at 1,372,500 to the dollar on the interbank market from 1,376,000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020508dy5800idg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
