\par\par \b \uc2  Curb On Bk Of Israel Powers Seen Prompting Intl Backlash \b0\par\par\uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 08:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (This item was originally run March 10 at 1647 GMT.)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Amy Teibel\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Finance Ministry's proposal to curb the Bank of Israel's powers threatens to unleash a harsh response by the international financial community, critics said Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Even those analysts who favor stripping Israel's central banker of his sole authority to set monetary policy termed the proposal misguided. \par \par \uc2  "This is an attempt to fully politicize the Bank of Israel, to take over fully the control of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a senior economist said on condition of anonymity. \par \par \uc2  "...It's a very tricky and treacherous road that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has decided to venture into," he said. "And hopefully there will be some people from the international financial community who will be able to point out the risks of playing around with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence." \par \par \uc2  The mainstay of the proposed amendment to the 1954 Bank of Israel Law, which the ministry submitted to Cabinet on Sunday, is formation of a nine-member monetary committee to set Israel's discount rate. \par \par \uc2  The committee, headed by the governor but nominated by the finance minister, would include the central banker's two deputies plus "six prominent economic figures or academics known for their monetary, financial or macroeconomic experience." \par \par \uc2  The ministry proposal also would give the government license to subordinate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mission of preserving price stability to growth and employment targets, and to change inflation targets mid-year. Additionally, it would let the finance minister direct the investment of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, and allow the government to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which supports the formation of a professional board of governors devoid of vested interests, warned of an international backlash in its attack on the proposal. \par \par \uc2  "The proposal does away with Israel's commitment to price stability, damages the Bank of Israel's independence, and subordinates the Bank of Israel to the directive of the finance minister," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  "This proposed legislation is liable to lead to a lowering of Israel's credit rating, given the expected deviation in the government's budget deficit, the downgrade in 2002 growth forecasts, and the grave security situation," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  A ratings downgrade would encourage capital outflows and thereby lead to higher domestic interest rates and financial destabilization, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par           Stock Exchange Unfazed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Tel Aviv Stock Exchange didn't react harshly to the news.\par Politicians have made similar proposals before, brokers noted, even\par though previous bills wouldn't have so sharply limited the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's powers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government never did anything with a professional committee's\par December 1998 proposal to overhaul the Bank of Israel Law, which\par included the establishment of a monetary committee and a clear statement\par of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's mandate of preserving price stability.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market doesn't trade on Sunday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The draft legislation, which Cabinet is to discuss next Sunday, comes\par at a time when the economy is stagnating, the budget deficit is\par ballooning, and the Bank of Israel is considering raising rates again\par after a 200-basis-point cut fueled price rises.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Minister Silvan Shalom, furious that the Dec. 25 rate cut was\par negotiated behind his back, is no less happy with the notion of rate\par rises, calling them a hindrance to growth and job creation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think that the government, and particularly the minister of\par finance, is worried that the economy is going to look bad and he's\par trying to clutch some straws to avoid sinking," the economist said. "And\par evidently those straws are in the form of irresponsible monetary policy\par and high inflation as something that is supposed to be a magic cure for\par GDP growth and unemployment."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The finance minister likely hopes the draft legislation will curb any\par planned rate rises in the short term, and in the longer term, "cause the\par Bank of Israel to be another department within the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,"\par he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If the government wants to administer monetary policy, "you don't need\par the Bank of Israel at all," a banking source said on condition of\par anonymity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This would very much weaken the Bank of Israel," he said. "I'm\par certainly not enthusiastic about this."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - By Amy Teibel; Dow Jones Newswires; 972-2-537-6985;\par amy.teibel@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020311dy3b000cr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
