\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Israel shekel sinks 1.4 percent vs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2002\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Feb 11 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel weakened 1.4 percent against the dollar in early trading on Monday, as lack of Bank of Israel action to stem the shekel's slide continued to spur heavy demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel moved above 4.73 to the dollar - its weakest point ever - immediately after opening, from Friday's representative rate of 4.6670. Monday's decline brings the shekel's losses to nearly 10 percent in the past seven weeks. \par \par \uc2  "The market feels that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market so there is a feeling of further appreciation in the dollar," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  By late morning, the shekel had recovered somewhat, to 4.72 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted that much of the shekel's drop has come from the general public selling shekel assets through mutual funds. \par \par \uc2  The shekel has been in virtual freefall against the dollar since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed its key lending rate by two percentage points to an all-time low of 3.8 percent on December 23. \par \par \uc2  "With the interest rate differential (slim versus U.S. rates) the attraction of holding shekels is limited," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The interest rate differential between Israel and the United States - whose federal funds rate stands at 1.75 percent - narrowed to 2.05 points from more than four points six weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  The Hapoalim dealer described the shekel's skid as a "snowball effect." \par \par \uc2  "People have been waiting for the dollar to retrace lower so they can buy at cheaper levels," he said. "But a lot of people missed the opportunity to buy at lower levels and now don't want to miss any further (shekel) depreciation." \par \par \uc2  Until the Bank of Israel's steep cut in late December - which came as part of a deal with the Finance Ministry to cut the budget - the shekel had held mostly steady, falling only marginally against the dollar in 2001 after appreciating in 2000. \par \par \uc2  But despite an initial slide in the shekel, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained mostly mum. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not likely to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, since it believes the market is too large to fight. \par \par \uc2  Instead, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be forced to raise interest rates should the consumer price index for January, which will be issued on Friday, shows a pop in inflation. \par \par \uc2  "If the CPI is very high (Bank of Israel Governor David Klein) may use that as an excuse to raise rates slightly," the Hapoalim dealer said. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2   ). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020211dy2b00i2d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
