\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel hits new low on Dec rate cut. \b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2002\par 15:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Jan 3 (Reuters) - The Israeli shekel weakened by 0.8 percent against the dollar in heavy trading on Thursday, setting yet another new low as the market continued to react to a sharp interest rate cut in late December, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel's representative rate was set at 4.4730 against the dollar compared with a previous low of 4.4370 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Demand for dollars has been very strong and this trend is expected to continue," said Guy Levy of Citibank in Tel Aviv. "There are sellers here or there but we don't yet see equilibrium in the market. My guess is this could happen at around 4.55." \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor David Klein said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market despite the shekel's weakening of some 4.6 percent in the past two weeks to a record low against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Klein said there was no danger of prices rising due to the shekel's weakness since the economy was in a recession. \par \par \uc2  The dollar strengthened to as high as 4.485 against the shekel during the day before falling back slightly. \par \par \uc2  "Trading has been very stormy," said a dealer at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  Levy also said there could be a correction at some point. "The question is when will this happen," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the broader public was buying dollars, both individually and through funds. In the past two weeks the shekel has lost 4.5 percent against the dollar, pressured by the Bank of Israel's interest rate reduction of two percentage points on December 23. \par \par \uc2  The cut brought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key lending rate to an historic low of 3.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  The shekel in recent months had been underpinned by the large interest rate spread with U.S. rates but since the Bank of Israel's cut last week the spread has narrowed to just 2.05 points. \par \par \uc2  The shekel's representative rate against the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was fixed at 4.5437 compared with 4.5050 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel was set at 3.3944 shekels per 100 yen compared with 3.3630, against the euro at 4.0474 shekels compared with 4.0062, and against the pound at 6.4653 shekels compared with 6.4212. \par \par \uc2  In late trading after the setting of the representative rate, the shekel traded at 4.4765 shekels per dollar. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2   ). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020103dy1300rbz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
