\par\par \b \uc2  Israel June Discount Rate Cut Again, Dn 20 BPs To 6.8% \b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2001\par 15:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM -(Dow Jones)- Making up for a skipped rate cut in May, the Bank of Israel said Monday it will cut the discount rate for a second time in June, to 6.8% from 7%, effective Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Governor David Klein canceled the May rate announcement because of labor unrest at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying he was denied data critical to setting policy. But when the bank announced the first June discount rate cut of 20 basis points in late May, it signaled that another reduction would follow if the unrest stopped, as it did last week. \par \par \uc2  Klein plans an announcement on the July discount rate in one week, resuming the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's regular once-a-month decision making process. He's expected to cut the July rate some 20 basis points. \par \par \uc2  The stock and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were unaffected by the expected modest credit softening. \par \par \uc2  Klein told Israel radio the rate reduction was designed to help stimulate growth without heating up inflation. Inflation expectations two years out aren't far below government targets, so "it is best to act prudently" when lowering rates, he said, signaling an intention to maintain his policy of small cuts. \par \par \uc2  In a release announcing the cut, Klein said rate changes to meet the inflation target won't offset the recessionary influence of the U.S. economic slowdown and renewed political violence at home, nor structural problems. \par \par \uc2  He urged the government to spend more on programs promoting economic growth, while maintaining a commitment to the diminishing budget deficit targets set through 2003. \par \par \uc2  Economists forecast 2001 inflation at 2% or less, below the government's target range of 2.5%-3.5%. The economy is expected to grow only 1%-2% in 2001, entrenching unemployment of close to 9%. \par \par \uc2  Political pressure now compounds the economic data in favour of a cut, with Prime Minister Ariel Sharon telling a business forum last week that rates "should and will come down." \par \par \uc2  Klein deflected an Israel radio question on how long he could withstand the political pressure for deeper cuts. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel has cut the discount rate by a total of 1.4 percentage points over the past five months. \par \par \uc2  In the release, Klein also cautioned that failure to jettison the shekel trading band is liable to set off "a financial crisis of inestimable proportions," and "uncalled-for and distorted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry, which would have to approve such a move, opposes eliminating the band for fear that a free-floating shekel would depreciate sharply. \par \par \uc2  -By Amy Teibel, Dow Jones Newswires; 972 2 537 6985; amy.teibeldowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx6i02pft\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
