\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel at four-month high to dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2000\par 15:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Aug 21 (Reuters) - The Israeli shekel forged another four-month high against the dollar on Monday spurred by the Bank of Israel's renewed call to remove the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  With the shekel less than 3.0 percent away from the strongest point of the band - a mechanism that allows the shekel to fluctuate some 17 percent above and below a gradually depreciating midpoint - it may not be long before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor David Klein told Reuters on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  But buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would necessitate printing more shekels, thereby putting in danger the country's inflation target, he said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is jumpy on the back of Klein's comments, but it seems some people are looking at it as a good buying opportunity and that may be holding (the exchange rate) at these levels," said a dealer at Bank Hapoalim. \par \par \uc2  "There's some support at 4.03, but it's at a level where if that breaks (the dollar) could go much lower," he said. \par \par \uc2  Klein's call for abolishing the band has not been supported by the government in the past and a government source said on Monday that the issue was not currently on the agenda. \par \par \uc2  The shekel's representative rate against the dollar was set at 4.0310 from 4.0400 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Corporate sector customers were more involved in buying dollars while banks led sales on thin volumes, a dealer at Eurotrust said. \par \par \uc2  "If (Klein) gets rid of the band he will do it with a rate cut, because otherwise it will push the shekel stronger," the dealer said. "The market is ripe to head to 4.0 but the question is what will happen there." \par \par \uc2  The basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , comprising the dollar, euro, pound sterling and yen, was fixed at 4.1494 compared with 4.1705 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses, the shekel traded at 3.7250 shekels per 100 yen compared with 3.7093, against the euro at 3.6394 shekels compared with 3.6988, and against the pound at 6.0141 shekels compared with 6.0434 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2   ). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8l0aymt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
