\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  hedging instruments rise to $12 bln. \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2000\par 13:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, April 5 (Reuters) - The value of hedging instruments against \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate risk in Israel rose to $12 billion in the beginning of 2000 from $8.5 billion in 1998, the Bank of Israel said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The 2000 estimate represents an average of January and February figures. \par \par \uc2  The instruments include options and futures transactions, reflecting the total value of all contracts that have yet to expire expressed in dollars. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attributed the rise "to the public's increased awareness to (exchange rate risk), due to the process of easing the exchange rate policy and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market." \par \par \uc2  Exchange rate risk in Israel has increased with greater volatility in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market seen in recent years, especially with a gradual liberalisation of trade. \par \par \uc2  In late 1998, a shekel depreciation was deepened by customers with foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans who were forced to buy dollars on the spot to cover their positions. \par \par \uc2  Commercial banks hold the vast majority of hedging instruments while 22 percent are traded on the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  ((Jerusalem newsroom, +972-2-537-0502, jerusalem.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba00