\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Israel's Frenkel mum on report he will top IMF. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Michele Gershberg \par \uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2000\par 19:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Reuters) - Jacob Frenkel declined to say on Sunday, his last day as Bank of Israel governor, whether he had been tipped by European diplomats to replace Michel Camdessus as head of the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman for the Bank of Israel said neither Frenkel, 56, nor the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would comment on the speculation he would succeed Camdessus who steps down in a month. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel's departure as Bank of Israel governor, after more than eight years in office, left a void pending cabinet approval of David Klein, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director, chosen by Prime Minister Ehud Barak to take Frenkel's place. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel announced in mid-November he would resign on January 2, but postponed his departure at the request of Barak who asked for one more week to name a successor. \par \par \uc2  Barak is in the United States for peace talks with Syria and a spokeswoman in his office could not say when the government would vote on Klein's appointment, announced on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Klein, like Frenkel, is thought to hold a tight monetary policy aimed at curbing inflation. But some politicians, including Finance Minister Abraham Shohat, had hoped for a loosening of the reins that would jump-start economic growth. \par \par \uc2  In his first comment on the choice of Klein, Shohat told Israel's Channel Two Television: "It is no secret that I thought there were nominees more suitable for the matter. \par \par \uc2  "I am not saying it on the personal level against David Klein. I have no complaints against him. I think conceptually a different governor should have been appointed." \par \par \uc2  Israeli markets hailed news of Klein's appointment, with the shekel strengthening against the dollar slightly on Friday and major stock indices gaining over three percent on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  PARLIAMENT TO REVIEW MONETARY POLICY COUNCIL \par \par \uc2  Lawmaker Elie Goldschmidt of Barak's One Israel faction said the parliamentary finance committee which he heads would review on Monday a bill to dilute the powers of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor. \par \par \uc2  The bill, introduced several years ago by Shohat and other lawmakers, would establish a monetary policy council that would make interest rate decisions. Currently the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief has final authority over interest rate adjustments. \par \par \uc2  "I suggest we do not interpret this initiative as a lack of faith in the incoming Bank of Israel governor," Goldschmidt told Israel Radio. \par \par \uc2  "We are creating a wider platform for taking such critical decisions for the future of the economy without hurting the character, standing or importance of the governor," he said. \par \par \uc2  NO DECISION-MAKER IN THE INTERIM \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  days until Klein is voted in, \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be left without a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief for the first time since the institution was established. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel law only allows a previously appointed deputy governor to step into the number one post once a central banker leaves, but the deputy position has not been filled for more than a decade. \par \par \uc2  While routine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decisions can still be carried out without a chief, the choice to adjust interest rates or to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market ultimately rests with the Bank of Israel governor. \par \par \uc2  "If there is some kind of sudden shock to the markets there is no one to take decisions (until Klein takes office), but there is little chance that will happen," a banking source said. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, "the situation is much better now than if Frenkel had left a week ago," the source said. \par \par \uc2  "The markets already know that the next governor will continue in (Frenkel's) line and are calm, so there is less likelihood that there will need to be a response" in the form of monetary policymaking, the source said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1905kb7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
