\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli Ctrl Banker: Politics Won't Dictate Monetary Policy \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 1999\par 15:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Israel will pursue a monetary policy that is dictated by economic considerations and not domestic politics, Governor Jacob Frenkel told a delegation from the Institute of International Finance Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Given the uncertainty on global financial markets and parliament's failure to approve a 1999 budget, "the Bank of Israel will continue to take action to preserve and guarantee economic stability as defined by government targets," a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  release cited Frenkel telling the delegation. \par \par \uc2  "Interest rate policy therefore will continue to be administered according to the dictates of the economic agenda, irrespective of political schedules," he said. \par \par \uc2  Parliament recently voted to dissolve itself over deep divisions within the governing coalition which led among other things to a failure to pass a budget for 1999. Early elections have been called for May 17. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel also defended his decision to raise the discount rate to 13.5% from 9.5% in November, and not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when the shekel dropped sharply against the dollar in October. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tight monetary policy has been criticized by many Israeli economists as well as some foreign economic experts. In its annual report on Israel in December, the International Monetary Fund seemed to fault the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  for not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October, when the shekel lost 11% of its value against the dollar. The shekel has since regained much of the ground it lost. \par \par \uc2  The delegation from the Institute of International Finance, an organization made up of leading financial institutions, is in Israel preparing its annual report on the Israeli economy. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1430GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1o00jd8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
