\par\par \b \uc2  Legislators warm to Bank of Israel oversight bill. \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 1998\par 14:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Dec 8 (Reuters) - Israel's parliamentary finance committee voted on Tuesday to move forward with opposition-sponsored legislation that would create a board to oversee Bank of Israel monetary policy-making, currently concentrated in its governor's hands. \par \par \uc2  The bill, which is not supported by the government, will now be presented to the plenum for the first of three readings before it becomes law. \par \par \uc2  After lying in abeyance for more than a year, the bill gained new momentum after the Bank of Israel came under attack from politicians and many business leaders for its handling of the shekel's sharp depreciation in October. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  refused to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and in a bid to curb resulting inflation its governor, Jacob Frenkel, raised interest rates sharply. \par \par \uc2  The hike was seen by many politicians and manufacturers as excessive and at the expense of economic growth. Under the current law, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor has sole authority to set interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "Monetary decisions cannot be in the hands of one person," said Likud legislator Zeev Boim. "Frenkel is top notch but something as serious as monetary policy can't be left to one person." \par \par \uc2  But some legislators warned a board of governors could hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence. \par \par \uc2  "This bill is dangerous (because) it ties the hands of the governor and affects the independence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Michael Kleiner, a member of the finance committee who voted against the proposal. \par \par \uc2  "There will be a chain reaction that will lead to a lowering of Israel's credit rating, a drop in investment and thousands of people losing their jobs." \par \par \uc2  Frenkel has said he would support a council of governors so long as the governor appointed its members and the change was part of a larger revision of the Bank of Israel Law. \par \par \uc2  A government-appointed committee is currently evaluating a revised law, proposed by the Bank of Israel, that would define the bank's goals and objectives. \par \par \uc2  The committee is expected to present its recommendations toward the end of the month. ((Jerusalem newsroom, +972 2 537-0502, jerusalem.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duc802sz9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
