\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-IMF report favours Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By David Rosenberg \par \uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1998\par 21:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Dec 2 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  should consider limited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the International Monetary Fund (IMF) said in a report obtained by Reuters on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "It is desirable to avoid as far as possible abrupt changes in monetary conditions. In this context, it would be useful to continue to explore whether limited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... can be undertaken without unduly encouraging risky behaviour," the IMF said in its interim report on the Israeli economy. \par \par \uc2  The report also urged the Israeli government to keep to its 4-percent inflation target for 1999, saying a revision upward would raise inflationary expectations, unsettle financial markets and coax wages higher. \par \par \uc2  The report came a day after the cabinet agreed to defer a decision until the second half of January on whether to raise next year's inflation target. \par \par \uc2  The IMF report appeared to be critical of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in early October when the shekel lost nearly 10 percent of its value against the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Jacob Frenkel has said repeatedly that the bank's policy is ordinarily not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the depreciation caused inflation to surge higher in October, forcing the Bank of Israel to raise interest rates 4.0 percentage points over late October and early November. \par \par \uc2  The IMF said the rate hike had been successful in curbing inflationary expectations but it said the government should now focus on bringing rates down. \par \par \uc2  "Economic policies in the next few months should strive to establish conditions for a gradual easing of the monetary stance, without risking a rekindling of inflation or the re-emergence of pressure for a depreciation of the shekel," the IMF said. \par \par \uc2  The report also urged policymakers to continue efforts to lower the degree of concentration in the Israeli financial system. \par \par \uc2  It said Israeli banks should be divested of their smaller banking units. The government should also "encourage additional break-ups of financial conglomerates" and "facilitate entry by foreign banks." \par \par \uc2  The report also suggested some technical changes, among them for the government to set its inflation target according to underlying inflation. It said that would insulate policy from much of the volatility in headline inflation. \par \par \uc2  The IMF said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should consider stepping up financial requirements for the banking system by raising minimum capital requirements, requiring larger provisions and discouraging high dividend payouts. \par \par \uc2  "While there is no reason to be concerned about the soundness of the banking system, the increased volatility in financial markets and asset prices and the large share of credit in - or linked to - foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  justify heightened vigilance," the report said. \par \par \uc2  The IMF conceded that its positive outlook for the economy a year ago had not been realised. \par \par \uc2  It said, however, that Israel now stood to benefit from the weaker shekel, which should make the country's exports more competitive, so long as policy makers could prevent the depreciation from creating long-term inflation. \par \par \uc2  ((Jerusalem newsroom, +972 2 537-0502, jerusalem.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duc20386t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
