\par\par \b \uc2  Israel/Fin Min -2: Zilberfarb Criticizes Rate Rises \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1998\par 13:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  At the same cabinet session, Finance Ministry director-general Ben-Zion Zilberfarb criticized the Bank of Israel for relying only on higher interest rates to stabilize the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel has been criticized widely in \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  for raising interest rates instead of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in early October, when the shekel fell sharply against the dollar. Critics say the high interest rates will only deepen Israel's economic slowdown, now in its third year. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Israel's involvement as a market maker would have prevented big jumps in the exchange rate," added liquidity to the market and raised long-term stability, Zilberfarb said. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the Finance Ministry had asked it to, then the price rises that followed the shekel's depreciation would have been more moderate, he said. \par \par \uc2  Although the Finance Ministry agrees that routine Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is undesirable, neither is total abstinence from market involvement, which carries an economic price by failing to restore stability to the financial market, Zilberfarb said. \par \par \uc2  Zilberfarb concluded his speech with an appeal to the cabinet not to expand spending in the 1999 draft state budget and to sign "responsible" public sector wage agreements. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel told the cabinet that the Israeli economy's primary challenge is to stimulate economic growth. The only way to do that is to cap spending at the level set out in the 1999 draft state budget and reaffirm a commitment to low inflation, he said. \par \par \uc2  The governor advocates maintaining the 1999 inflation target of 4.0%. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel cautioned that if interest rates are cut too rapidly or the Bank of Israel's autonomy is undermined, Israel's financial stability and economic growth could be hurt. \par \par \uc2  He once again defended his decision to raise the key lending rate as an effort to prevent the recent surge in prices from becoming entrenched. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-12-98 \par \par \uc2  1234GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duc101om1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
