\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli Shekel Up Vs Dlr In Late Trade: Fixing At ILS4.1520 \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 1998\par 14:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The shekel (ILS) is higher against the dollar for the seventh consecutive trading day Tuesday as a newly widened gap between local and foreign interest rates is making dollar sales attractive for customers. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel fixed the shekel at ILS4.1520 to the dollar, up 0.2% from Monday's fixing at ILS4.1600. \par \par \uc2  The shekel traded within a range of ILS4.1200 to ILS4.1700 to the dollar. Shortly after the 1315 GMT fixing, the shekel was trading at ILS4.1500. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its key lending rate in November to 13.5% in two separate increases of 200 basis points each. Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel said the second surprise increase was meant to stem a wave of dollar buying on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and halt accelerating inflation. \par \par \uc2  "It was an hysterical response to the market coupled with (the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) determination not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading" to strengthen the shekel, one foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The consequent rise in real interest rates had customers selling dollars Tuesday, pushing the shekel as high as ILS4.1200 to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Trading volumes were moderate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel is scheduled to announce the December key lending rate on Monday. A Tel Aviv-based dealer said the market "isn't ruling out another rate rise, but at this point it's at the back of their minds." \par \par \uc2  Customers see another rate rise likely only in the event of the shekel weakening considerably against the dollar in the next week, to levels of ILS4.3000 or lower, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By Michele Gershberg;9722-537-6985;mgershberg@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-11-98 \par \par \uc2  1352GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dubh018eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
