\par\par \b \uc2  Israel finmin says will review inflation target. \b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 1998\par 14:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Nov 15 (Reuters) - Israeli Finance Minister Yaacov Neeman told a cabinet meeting on Sunday he would reexamine the government's 1999 inflation target, a Treasury spokesman. \par \par \uc2  "The finance minister thinks...there is reason to examine the need to change the inflation target in light of what has happened over the past month and a half," the spokesman said after the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Neeman agreed to study the matter after several ministers called for raising the target to between four and six percent after the shekel's slide against the dollar last month, which has led to higher inflation and a sharp hike in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The government is currently committed to a 4.0 percent inflation rate next year, down from a 1998 target of seven to 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  The year-end surge in inflation is expected to lift the full-year 1998 inflation rate to close to 10 percent. It was running at a four percent rate in the first eight months. \par \par \uc2  Sunday's cabinet meeting followed the Bank of Israel's surprise announcement on Thursday that it would hike the base lending rate by two percentage points for the second time in less than three weeks. The latest increase, effective on Sunday, brings the key lending rate to an annual 13.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel said the move was aimed at bringing inflation in line with the government's 1999 target of four percent. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel's tightening of monetary policy has led to an uproar in both the public and private sector and some leaders of the business sector have called for his resignation. \par \par \uc2  According to the Treasury spokesman, Neeman told the cabinet the Treasury had differences of opinion with the Bank of Israel but said it was inappropriate to make personal attacks on the governor because it challenged the authority of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The spokesman declined to detail the nature of these disagreements. But he said Neeman would elaborate on them during a special cabinet meeting later this week or next. \par \par \uc2  A senior Treasury source said the key dispute between the Finance Ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is over the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's failure to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The Treasury believes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should have taken place already to stem the shekel's decline. \par \par \uc2  Later on Sunday the government is due to publish October's consumer price index, which is expected to show a surge of three to four percent reflecting the brunt of a nearly 10 percent drop in the shekel against the dollar over the month. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubf04eum\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
