\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli Treasury says no plan to end shekel band. \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1998\par 11:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The Israeli Treasury on Wednesday denied press reports that it was in talks with the Bank of Israel to eliminate the shekel trading band following the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent sharp depreciation. \par \par \uc2  "There is no intention of changing the trading band - not at this stage," Treasury spokesman Moti Sherf told Reuters. "I don't want to discuss this because, if I do, it's as though it's on the agenda." \par \par \uc2  Israeli newspapers on Wednesday reported that Treasury officials had held talks with the Bank of Israel over the last few weeks over a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  proposal to eliminate the band. \par \par \uc2  The Ha'aretz newspaper said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believed removing the band would make it easier for it to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if it came under further pressure. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel declined to comment on the reports. \par \par \uc2  "We are not saying anything about this," a spokesman for the Bank of Israel said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel trades within a band set against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and straddles two sides of a sloping mid-point. The band has a width of 31.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Since the end of 1996, the shekel has traded close to the bottom, or stronger edge of the band. But in the last six weeks the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tumbled against the dollar and basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushing it towards the mid-point. \par \par \uc2  The shekel's slide and continued volatility has triggered calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it will not ordinarily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past has only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the trading band. \par \par \uc2  At midday on Wednesday, the shekel had strengthened to about 4.27 to the dollar from Monday's 4.301 fix. ((Jerusalem newsroom, +972 2 537-0502, jerusalem.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubb04vgd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
