\par\par \b \uc2  Israel Finance Ministry:Not Planning To Abolish Shekel Band \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 1998\par 17:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The Finance Ministry denied Tuesday that Israel's economic policymakers are discussing plans to abolish the shekel's trading band ($1=ILS4.3010). \par \par \uc2  "The Finance Ministry states that changing the exchange-rate policy isn't on the agenda. In light of the fact that the exchange rate now falls in the middle of the trading band, there is no need to change the band's limits," the ministry said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is allowed to fluctuate 15% on either side of a gradually depreciating midpoint. The Bank of Israel is committed to defending the upper and lower limits of the band. \par \par \uc2  The statement followed a report in the Yediot Ahronoth newspaper that said Finance Ministry officials are more likely to accept widening or even abolishing the trading band since the shekel lost more than 10.5% of its value against the dollar in October. \par \par \uc2  In addition, the report said, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials are stepping up discussions on abolishing the band to allow for more freedom of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't known to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trade in the last two months, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have repeatedly opposed regular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could invite speculative attacks on the Israeli market. \par \par \uc2  Removing the band, however, would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary to calm market volatility without significantly reducing market risk. Critics of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have called for some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trade to halt the shekel's slide and prevent an inflationary spiral. \par \par \uc2  Inflation estimates for 1998 have doubled since the depreciation occurred, with estimates running at around 9.0%, compared with earlier forecasts of 4.0% to 5.0%. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel refused to comment on the report. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry said it doesn't rule out using any tools necessary to adjust to developments on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but stressed "the authority to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade rests solely with the Bank of Israel." \par \par \uc2  -By Michele Gershberg; 9722-537-6985; mgershberg@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-11-98 \par \par \uc2  1622GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duba010mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
