\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  official defends  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  policy. \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 1998\par 12:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Nov 2 (Reuters) - A senior Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  official on Monday defended the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last month but left open the possibility it might act to moderate market volatility. \par \par \uc2  "There are situations when \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market can be considered as a way of moderating sharp daily fluctuations, but not in order to reverse the trend," David Klein, head of bank's monetary division, said in an article released to the press. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel has come under fire for failing to support the shekel during volatile trading in October when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed some 10.5 percent against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In response, the Bank of Israel last Monday announced a 2.0 percentage point hike in the base lending rate to 11.5 percent. In addition, the Treasury has stepped up auctions of dollar-linked bonds to try to soak up demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Klein cited the Bank of Israel's support of bond prices when the market collapsed in the summer of 1996 as an example of successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...helped the market to arrive at a new level of equilibrium that allowed it to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the report said. \par \par \uc2  "This was a successful measure because we were careful to allow the bond prices to drop in line with the market trend. The market knew that there was no absolute level at which we would bring the decline to a complete halt." \par \par \uc2  Klein ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reverse trends or to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the sly. \par \par \uc2  "Those who recommend that the Bank of Israel secretly sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would perhaps also recommend... doing this via futures contracts, without reporting them, which was done by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Thailand in 1997, before it broke its neck." \par \par \uc2  Klein warned that measuring the extent of demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was difficult and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  risked increasing demand by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ((Jerusalem newsroom, +972 2 537-0502, jerusalem.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dub205ll4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
