\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Bank of Israel raises interest rate to 11.5 pct. \b0\par\par\uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 1998\par 08:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Oct 26 (Reuters) - The Bank of Israel raised its key monetary tender rate for November to 11.5 percent on Monday, hiking it by a full two percentage points in response to a slump in the value of the shekel and a sudden surge in inflation. \par \par \uc2  "This is an exceptional rise in the interest rate and the circumstances are exceptional," \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Jacob Frenkel told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  He said the move was designed to help ensure that the government would meet its 1999 inflation target of four percent and again ruled out repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , calling it inefficient. \par \par \uc2  Frenkel blamed "dramatic" global conditions for sparking the first interest rate rise in more than a year and said the increase was intended as a "cure for the illness and to restore stability so that for 1999 we will return to inflation equal to four percent as determined by the government". \par \par \uc2  The decision was announced at 8.30 a.m. (0630 GMT), eight hours earlier than is normally the case, so that markets would be able to trade on the basis of the new figure. \par \par \uc2  The shekel strengthened against the dollar in very early trading in Tel Aviv but then pulled back on profit taking following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement. \par \par \uc2  At 0705 GMT, the shekel was at 4.2201 to the dollar, compared with its 4.2490 fix on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The market basically opened lower for the dollar. We traded around 4.16 before the announcement from the governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Yaacov Harpaz, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at United Mizrahi Bank. \par \par \uc2  Harpaz said the interest rate differential between the shekel and dollar had widened. He said the rate hike, which was at the higher end of analysts' expectations, would help steady the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I think it will be stabilising in the range in 4.10-4.25," he said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel has been falling against the dollar since August. The pace quickened in an increasingly volatile market during October and then last Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record low against the dollar of 4.367. \par \par \uc2  The shekel's losses have quickly upset expectations that annual inflation would fall below four percent this year and there are fears it could cause further damage in 1999 unless checked. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts expect the consumer price index in October alone to rise by about 3.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Amir Haik, chief analyst at Israel Union Bank, said on Sunday that even if the shekel stabilised at between 4.1 and 4.2 to the dollar, 1999 inflation would be five to six percent, well above the government's 4.0 percent target. \par \par \uc2  In the last three years, the Bank of Israel has changed the direction of interest rates three times. It had cut the base rate a total of 3.9 points in the first eight months of this year. The last rate rise was in August 1997. \par \par \uc2  Economists are divided about the preference for raising rates over direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a mechanism Frenkel reiterated on Monday was not on the cards. \par \par \uc2  "In current conditions, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on a daily and sustained basis...in order to preserve the exchange rate is inefficient and cannot substitute for an interest rate policy," Frenkel said. \par \par \uc2  ((Jerusalem newsroom, +972 2 537-0502, jerusalem.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113duaq02kp2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
