\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: Israel Rate Rise -3: Will Hit 1999 Growth \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 1998\par 16:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The government approved the 4.0% inflation target after inflation expectations for the first half of 1999 had dropped to a low of 3.5% to 4.5% by the end of July. But following the depreciation, analysts now forecast 1998 inflation between 6.0% and 9.0%, and project a 5.0% to 7.0% increase for 1999. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said strategic and discrete \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market may have served the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the economy, better. But a declared \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have increased a sense of panic in the market and invited speculative dollar-buying, Gutman said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  critics said the 200 basis point increase will only deepen the country's slowdown and worsen unemployment, forecast between 9.0% and 9.5% for 1998. \par \par \uc2  "The discount rate rise ruins any chance to renew growth at the start of 1999," said Doron Tamir, vice president of the Manufacturer's Association of Israel. Growth in 1998 is forecast at 1.5%, while 1999 projections have been lowered to a range of 2.0% to 2.5% from 2.5%. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think we need to give priority to another decline in inflation over a decline in unemployment at this time," Ben-Bassat said. "The drop to 4.0% inflation was to a certain degree unsustainable," because it was kept down through artificial exchange rate levels that resulted from the high interest rate policy, he said. \par \par \uc2  "A decline to 7.0% inflation is a little more convincing (for 1999)," he said. \par \par \uc2  -By Michele Gershberg;9722-537-6985;mgershberg@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 26-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1504GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duaq00ft0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
