\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli Shekel/Rate Rise -3:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Preferred \b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 1998\par 16:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Sheinen and others argue the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the shekel, even though it's still some 11.4% from the floor of its trading band. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is allowed to fluctuate in a band of plus or minus 15% from a gradually depreciating midpoint. \par \par \uc2  "It's not like Southeast Asia or Russia because the Israeli economy isn't in a state that requires such a depreciation," Sheinen said. "It's leading to upheavals we don't need." \par \par \uc2  Because Israel is a small, import-reliant market, it's vulnerable to swings in exchange rates, he said. \par \par \uc2  "We need a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that will moderate the fluctuations," Sheinen said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel had been kept artificially strong over the last four years as the Bank of Israel kept interest rates high in an effort to tame inflation. \par \par \uc2  But the shekel's over valuation was only in the range of 10% to 15%, not the 20% by which it has fallen since August, said Sheinen. If the Bank of Israel doesn't stabilize the market, inflation in 1998 could surge above 10%, he cautioned. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a major Israeli trading room said he thought the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  should have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market first in words, then in deed. \par \par \uc2  "They should have said 4.2 shekels to the dollar is a good level for the Israeli economy, and then if needed, added some liquidity to the market" by selling dollars, he said on condition of anonymity. \par \par \uc2  -By Amy Teibel (972-2) 537 6985 ateibel@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1429GMT \par \par \uc2  1193 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duam00eki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
