\par\par \b \uc2  Analysts split on reasons for Israeli shekel's fall. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jennifer Friedlin \par \uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 1998\par 17:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Oct 21 (Reuters) - The battered Israeli shekel has been careering lower for some three weeks, but analysts still can't agree on who is in the driver's seat. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers point to foreign banks for the 13 percent slide in the shekel against the dollar since the start of October. But others insist it is nervous Israelis. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday the shekel was fixed at a record low against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 4.355. \par \par \uc2  A senior dealer at Israel Continental Bank said overseas institutions were testing the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with the knowledge that they would be losing trading opportunities when the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is introduced on January 1. \par \par \uc2  "With the euro taking away a lot of business, foreigners are looking for business," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "They are looking to see how much money they can make in this market, if they can do a little bit of manipulating and how much of a multiplier effect they can have." \par \par \uc2  But Nadine Baudot-Trajtenberg, of Bank Hapoalim's securities research and international marketing division, said domestic players had triggered the recent round of losses. \par \par \uc2  She said the atmosphere of uncertainty was causing domestic investors to pile into dollar-linked investments, while Israeli companies were seeking to refinance \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -linked loans. \par \par \uc2  Global economic uncertainty had turned foreigners off from speculating in the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, she argued. \par \par \uc2  "Given the dramatic turn in the world crisis, a lot of companies are scared of playing the shekel," Baudot-Trajtenberg said. "They thought they could play Russia and they learned they couldn't." \par \par \uc2  Despite the lack of consensus on reasons for the shekel's recent weakness several analysts said the time had come for the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I don't really understand why the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order not to have to change the interest rates," said Ed Butchart, an economist and market strategist for Merrill Lynch in London. \par \par \uc2  He said a steep increase in interest rates would hurt investment but that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market could help offset inflationary pressure resulting from the shekel depreciation. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Israel Governor Jacob Frenkel has indicated several times this month that he would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market unless the shekel reached the edge of its trading band against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The shekel is currently at about the mid-point. \par \par \uc2  That means the shekel would have to weaken a further 15 percent before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Butchart said that before the shekel's most recent drops he expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise interest rates by 0.5 percentage point when it announces November rates on Monday, but he would have to reassess that forecast after the shekel's recent losses. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Israel's base monetary tender rate is now 9.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Pinchas Landau, head of Euro Strategies Ltd, said the Bank of Israel should launch a "pre-emptive attack" in order to defend the shekel. \par \par \uc2  "Because of the very uncertain situation, right now is the time to do it (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), before things get out of control," Landau said. ((Jerusalem newsroom, +972 2 537-0502, jerusalem.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113dual02b50\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
