\par\par \b \uc2  Israel/Shekel -2: Thin Volumes Amplify Dlr's Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 1998\par 14:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM (Dow Jones)--The shekel (ILS) is trading lower against the dollar in thin trading midday Tuesday as customers await a rise in interest rates for November. \par \par \uc2  At 1145 GMT, the shekel was trading within a range of ILS4.2700 to ILS4.3150 to the dollar, down from Monday's Bank of Israel fixing at ILS4.2370. \par \par \uc2  Trading was thin and volumes low, strengthening the impact of individual purchases on the dollar's rise, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. Many regular customers were inactive and banks weren't taking strong positions in either direction, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Many people are waiting for the discount rate announcement. It looks like there will be a one percentage point increase, because a 50 basis point rise has been factored into the market and won't be enough" to calm trading, one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is scheduled to announce the November discount rate on Monday. The current rate is 9.5%. \par \par \uc2  The shekel has dropped more than 10% since the end of September, touching off price rises and fears of an inflationary spiral. Inflation estimates for 1998 are now as high as 8.0%, compared with previous estimates of 4.0% to 5.0% at the end of August. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic policy makers have pledged not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and dealers said their statements have not sent a calming signal to customers. \par \par \uc2  A report in the Ha'aretz newspaper Tuesday said the market feared the Bank of Israel would abolish the shekel's trading band. Dealers said Tuesday they didn't see that trading was affected by the rumor. \par \par \uc2  The shekel is allowed to fluctuate 15% on either side of a gradually depreciating midpoint, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is committed to defending the upper and lower limits of that band. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman wasn't immediately available for comment on the newspaper report. \par \par \uc2  -By Michele Gershberg;9722-537-6985;mgershberg@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-10-98 \par \par \uc2  1217GMT \par \par \uc2  1092 1849 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duak00a37\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
