\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Israel - Oct 11. \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 1998\par 08:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM, Oct 11 (Reuters) - These are some of the leading stories in Israeli newspapers on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  YEDIOTH AHRONOTH \par \par \uc2  - Ahead of the Wye Plantation summit to hammer out a peace deal with Palestinians, Foreign Minister-designate Ariel Sharon imposes constraints on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. If there is a deal, Sharon will oppose it. \par \par \uc2  - Sharon favours not a comprehensive peace with the Palestinians but rather a non-belligerency deal for a few dozen years with each side getting about half of the West Bank. \par \par \uc2  - Contacts under way to arrange for U.S. President Bill Clinton's participation in the Middle East in an Israeli-Palestinian signing ceremoney. \par \par \uc2  - Dollar falls to 4.26 shekels. \par \par \uc2  - Scitex warns it expects loss of $10-15 million in third quarter 1998. \par \par \uc2  MAARIV \par \par \uc2  - Sharon's appointment draws mix of reaction: National Religious Party satisfied, the left goes on attack, Arabs criticise, Palestinians are cautious. In Jerusalem it's expected Clinton will force a handshake between Sharon and Arafat. \par \par \uc2  - In rare move Netanyahu to leave wife Sara at home at request of Americans who say it's a closed and crowded meeting they're planning. \par \par \uc2  JERUSALEM POST \par \par \uc2  - Palestinian President Yasser Arafat cautious over Foreign Ministry nod to Ariel Sharon. \par \par \uc2  - Woman soldier stabbed to death in Jordan Valley. \par \par \uc2  - Histadrut trade union federation chairman Amir Peretz seeks to have workers compensated for salary erosion following the depreciation of the shekel. \par \par \uc2  HA'ARETZ \par \par \uc2  - Soldier's killer "acted alone," has history of mental illness. \par \par \uc2  - Sharon to act as "watchdog over Netanyahu" at summit. \par \par \uc2  - Yitzhar settlers in West Bank open fire on Palestinians and Israelis. \par \par \uc2  - Finance Minister Yaacov Neeman has ruled out any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  - Public apathy turns into worry despite shekel's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  - Treasury predicts 1.1 percent consumer price index gain in September. \par \par \uc2  - Israel's recession-struck diamond industry has moved a step closer to collapse with the imminent breakdown of Lorenzii Diamonds' creditor arrangement. \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 4.26 shekels) ((Jerusalem newsroom: 972 2 537 0502; jerusalem.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113duab01muf\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (israel near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clve